5a. What Hermes Is (resolving the v1 ambiguity)
Hermes is a deterministic/statistical decision layer, not a free-reasoning LLM agent:

Strategy proposals come from rule-based or statistically-fitted models (e.g. the momentum/breakout/mean-reversion family, or future validated alternatives) with fixed, versioned parameters — not from an LLM interpreting context at decision time.
Any LLM in the system is restricted to the read-only market-intelligence/news layer (summarization and classification only, as already scoped in your fourth external review), never to producing the action, confidence, or decision_rationale fields directly.
The confidence field in the Decision object (§9) is a calibrated statistical output (e.g. proposal agreement rate, historical hit rate of the triggering condition) — not a model's self-reported certainty. decision_rationale is template-generated from structured evidence, not free text, so it stays reproducible and backtestable.
This matters because Section 26's testing strategy (deterministic reproducibility, no look-ahead) is only achievable if the decision layer itself is deterministic given the same inputs. An LLM making per-cycle trading calls would silently break that guarantee.

5b. Edge Validation Gate (new — blocking)
No strategy, old or new, may appear in strategies/ (§8) or receive a production strategy-version ID (§17) without passing this gate.

Already-falsified strategies (permanently recorded, cannot re-enter without a materially different hypothesis — not just retuned parameters):

Strategy family	Status	Evidence
Breakout (24/12/14 lookback, hourly)	FALSIFIED	Phase 0: net return −27.78%, bootstrap CI entirely negative
Scalping (5/3/14 lookback, 1-min)	FALSIFIED	Phase 0: net return −39.42%, bootstrap CI entirely negative
Breakout + ADX>25 filter	FALSIFIED	Phase 0b: improved headline (−5.87%) but failed pre-registered replication (bull-market-dependent)
Breakout + magnitude≥0.5×ATR filter	FALSIFIED	Phase 0b: improved headline (−2.84%) but failed replication
Breakout + volume>20SMA filter	FALSIFIED	Phase 0b: NO CREDIBLE EDGE
Corrected baseline (intrabar stop-loss fix)	FALSIFIED	Phase 0b: −26.48%
Section 8's strategy list (Momentum, Trend Following, Breakout, Mean Reversion, VWAP Reversion, Order Flow) therefore cannot be built as-is. Trend Following, Mean Reversion, VWAP Reversion and Order Flow have not yet been tested against this bar on crypto data and remain candidates — but only through this gate, not by default inclusion.

Gate requirements for any candidate (new or revived):

Hypothesis and acceptance criteria pre-registered in research/reports/EXPERIMENT_REGISTRY.md before seeing test-period results.
Backtest on a fresh holdout period never used in prior experiments.
Net of realistic fees, slippage, and India VDA tax treatment (30% on transfer gains, no loss offset, 1% TDS as a cash-flow drag).
Bootstrap confidence interval reported; must exclude zero on the positive side to pass.
Regime-robustness check across at least two structurally different periods (e.g. trending vs. range-bound, as already done for the momentum family in Steps 9–11).
Internal replication check: if a filter or refinement improves headline numbers, it must be tested on data outside the period it was tuned on before being credited.
A null result is accepted as a legitimate, final outcome for that hypothesis — no unlimited retry loop against the same holdout.
Only strategies that pass all seven criteria are eligible to be added to strategies/ as a versioned module.

6. Hermes Continuous Observation Loop
Hermes should not repeatedly ask an LLM to interpret thousands of raw events. The market-data service already performs normalization and deterministic feature computation. (See §5a — this applies to the entire decision path, not just event volume.)

Recommended flow:

Receive market events and periodic snapshots.
Check freshness, completeness and contradiction status.
Update the active market context for each tracked symbol.
Detect regime changes or meaningful state transitions.
Trigger strategy evaluation at controlled intervals and on important events — using only gate-approved strategies.
Generate strategy proposals independently.
Evaluate proposals against current portfolio/risk state and historical strategy performance.
Produce BUY/SELL/HOLD with an explicit expiry time.
Send BUY/SELL only through deterministic risk validation.
Persist the decision and all structured evidence.
