17. Continuous Learning Architecture (revised)
Learning must be controlled. A single loss must never automatically rewrite the live strategy — and a candidate strategy version may never skip the Edge Validation Gate (§5b) on its way back to production, regardless of how it was generated.

Closed Trade → Trade Analysis → Candidate Lesson → Candidate Strategy Version
→ EDGE VALIDATION GATE (fresh holdout, pre-registered criteria)
→ Backtest → Paper Simulation → Evaluation → Promotion → Production Strategy Version
Every strategy version is immutable. Every production decision records its strategy version. Candidate versions remain isolated from live trading. Rollback must be possible instantly. A strategy can be disabled without deleting its history.

