21. Failure Handling and Safety
(Unchanged from v1, plus one line.)

If market data is stale/incomplete: HOLD/no new entry.
If cross-exchange data is contradictory beyond tolerance: reduce confidence or HOLD.
If risk service is unavailable: no execution.
If n8n is unavailable: expire requests, do not queue indefinitely.
If Binance execution state cannot be reconciled: freeze new entries and reconcile.
If database persistence fails: stop new trading rather than operate without an audit trail.
If Hermes becomes unhealthy: supervisor restarts it and verifies state from durable storage.
If daily loss/drawdown limit is reached: activate kill switch.
If strategy version validation fails: keep the existing production version.
If a strategy's edge_validation_records reference is missing or its parameters have drifted from what was gated: treat as a risk error (§16) and halt that strategy immediately.
On restart: rebuild portfolio state from exchange reconciliation plus durable local records.
