29. Recommended First Implementation Step (revised)
Do not start with Hermes Foundation, and do not start by connecting live Binance execution. The next implementation step is Phase 0: run Trend Following, Mean Reversion, VWAP Reversion, and Order Flow through the same pre-registered, fresh-holdout, cost-and-tax-adjusted testing regime that already falsified Breakout and Scalping. Only once at least one strategy family produces a bootstrap CI that excludes zero on the positive side, survives a regime-robustness check, and replicates out-of-sample, does it make sense to begin Hermes Foundation with that strategy as its first wired module. Building the observer/context/decision/risk/execution scaffolding before that point produces a system with nothing valid to decide.

30. End-to-End Target Flow (revised)
A candidate strategy passes the Edge Validation Gate on a fresh holdout, or the project reaches a documented null result.
Market-data service continuously collects and validates real-time data.
Hermes receives current snapshots and important events.
Hermes builds structured context for each candidate symbol.
Only gate-approved strategies generate proposals.
Hermes evaluates proposals, historical performance and portfolio state.
Hermes creates an auditable BUY/SELL/HOLD decision with an expiry, deterministically (§5a).
Deterministic risk validates the decision and computes exact approved quantity/protection.
Only an approved ExecutionRequest is sent to n8n.
n8n validates and submits the request to Binance.
Order/fill events are reconciled into the local lifecycle.
Position monitoring tracks the open position until closure.
Closed trades are analyzed against the original thesis and execution.
Candidate mistakes/lessons are stored.
Candidate strategy changes re-enter through the Edge Validation Gate before backtest/paper-test.
Validated strategy versions can be promoted and rolled back.
Hermes loads the active strategy versions and continues the loop 24/7.
31. Final Architecture Principle
The system should be autonomous in operation, but not uncontrolled — and it should not be built before it has something real to operate on. Hermes is responsible for observation, analysis and deterministic decisioning; the Edge Validation Gate is responsible for making sure that decisioning has a real basis; deterministic risk is responsible for safety; n8n is responsible for execution orchestration; Binance is the execution venue; the trade analyzer is responsible for learning from outcomes; and the database provides the durable memory and audit trail connecting every step.

The desired end state is not simply an AI that predicts BUY or SELL. It is a closed-loop trading operating system in which every market observation, edge-validation attempt, strategy proposal, decision, risk check, execution, fill, position, trade outcome, lesson and strategy version can be reconstructed, evaluated and improved in a controlled manner — and in which no component downstream of the gate can ever run on an unvalidated strategy.

